>About

Marcus Strauss. Southern Ontario.

>>Now
 - Studying Software Development & Network Engineering at Sheridan College
 - Running Strauss AI, a small automation consultancy (the clearnet one lives at
   straussai.ca)
 - Poking at networks that don't need the internet

>>Before
Tech support at an ISP: fiber, coax, WiFi, VoIP, and a lot of patient explaining.
It left me curious about what the network looks like underneath, which is how I
ended up here, on one that doesn't use IP at all.

>>Why a mesh node
Because it's the most interesting way I've found to learn what addressing, routing,
and trust actually are: take them away and rebuild them from keys.

